{"tool_name":"paa","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"paa","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/PAA","license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"PAA imports single color (protein) microarray data that has been saved in gpr file format - esp. ProtoArray data. After preprocessing (background correction, batch filtering, normalization) univariate feature preselection is performed (e.g., using the \"minimum M statistic\" approach - hereinafter referred to as \"mMs\"). Subsequently, a multivariate feature selection is conducted to discover biomarker candidates. Therefore, either a frequency-based backwards elimination aproach or ensemble feature selection can be used. PAA provides a complete toolbox of analysis tools including several different plots for results examination and evaluation.","addition_date":"2016-07-12T09:35:15Z","last_update_date":"2026-08-30T02:26:29.297870Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.46.0"],"collections":["BioConductor","BioInfra.Prot","Proteomics","de.NBI"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:paa","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"name":"Martin Eisenacher","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Contributor","Maintainer"]},{"name":"Michael Turewicz","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer","Maintainer"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/PAA"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Raw microarray data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3110"}},{"data":{"term":"Text","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3671"},"format":[{"term":"TSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3475"}]}],"note":"Biomarker discovery with protein microarrays PAA imports raw microarray data from files in gpr file format. Experiment description List of selected biomarker candidates (UniProtKB accessions) including all related information (such as their sequences p-values and fold changes). PAA 